### Apni Dukan API: click ▶ next to a request (environment "local"). See http/README.md.
# Your phone, email and the codes you receive (otp, emailCode) go in http-client.private.env.json, which Git ignores,
# so nothing personal is ever committed from this file. The file id is saved automatically by request 7.

### 1. Send OTP (SMS through MSG91). Once TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY is set (the real server), add "captchaToken" from the
### app's Turnstile widget; on your laptop it isn't needed.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/otp/send
Content-Type: application/json

{ "phone": "{{phone}}" }

### 2. Verify OTP → signs in (creates the account the first time). Saves the tokens.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/otp/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{ "phone": "{{phone}}", "code": "{{otp}}", "device": "IntelliJ" }

> {%
    client.test("Signed in", () => client.assert(response.status === 200, "Status " + response.status));
    client.global.set("accessToken", response.body.accessToken);
    client.global.set("refreshToken", response.body.refreshToken);
%}

### 3. Who am I
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 4. Refresh: new pair, the old refresh token is used up. Saves the new tokens.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}" }

> {%
    client.global.set("accessToken", response.body.accessToken);
    client.global.set("refreshToken", response.body.refreshToken);
%}

### 5. Send an email code (Gmail)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/email/send-code
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}" }

### 5b. Replacing an already verified email: first a code to your own phone (then add "phoneCode" in request 5)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/email/change-phone-code
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 6. Verify the email with the code from your inbox
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/email/verify
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}", "code": "{{emailCode}}" }

### 6b. Register your shop (step 1). Then run request 4 (Refresh) so your token carries the shop.
POST {{baseUrl}}/shops
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Sharma Kirana Store",
  "ownerName": "Ramesh Sharma",
  "addressLine": "Shop 4, Lake View Apartments",
  "area": "Kondapur",
  "city": "Hyderabad",
  "pincode": "500084",
  "latitude": 17.465123,
  "longitude": 78.364456
}

### 6b-salon. Or register your shop as a salon (instead of 6b). Then run request 4 (Refresh).
POST {{baseUrl}}/shops
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Sharma Hair Studio",
  "ownerName": "Ramesh Sharma",
  "addressLine": "Shop 4, Lake View Apartments",
  "area": "Kondapur",
  "city": "Hyderabad",
  "pincode": "500084",
  "latitude": 17.465123,
  "longitude": 78.364456,
  "type": "SALON"
}

### 6c. My shop (details, status, type KIRANA or SALON, your role, version)
GET {{baseUrl}}/shops/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

> {%
    client.global.set("shopVersion", response.body.version);
%}

### 6d. Edit My shop (owner only): send the version from 6c and only what changes
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/shops/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "version": {{shopVersion}}, "name": "Sharma General Store" }

> {%
    if (response.status === 200) {
        client.global.set("shopVersion", response.body.version);
    }
%}

### 6e. Salon (registered with 6b-salon): add a service (owner only)
POST {{baseUrl}}/salon/services
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Haircut", "durationMinutes": 30, "pricePaise": 15000, "priceIsFrom": false, "sortOrder": 0 }

> {%
    if (response.status === 201) {
        client.global.set("serviceId", response.body.id);
    }
%}

### 6f. Salon: the services list
GET {{baseUrl}}/salon/services
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 6g. Salon: add a barber
POST {{baseUrl}}/salon/staff
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Raju" }

> {%
    if (response.status === 201) {
        client.global.set("staffId", response.body.id);
        client.global.set("staffVersion", response.body.version);
    }
%}

### 6h. Salon: what this barber does (replaces the list; send his version from 6g or the last reply)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/salon/staff/{{staffId}}/services
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "version": {{staffVersion}}, "serviceIds": ["{{serviceId}}"] }

> {%
    if (response.status === 200) {
        client.global.set("staffVersion", response.body.version);
    }
%}

### 6i. Salon: his week (replaces it). Monday split shift, Sunday to midnight
PUT {{baseUrl}}/salon/staff/{{staffId}}/hours
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "version": {{staffVersion}}, "hours": [
    { "weekday": 1, "start": "10:00", "end": "14:00" },
    { "weekday": 1, "start": "16:00", "end": "21:00" },
    { "weekday": 7, "start": "12:00", "end": "24:00" }
] }

> {%
    if (response.status === 200) {
        client.global.set("staffVersion", response.body.version);
    }
%}

### 6j. Salon: booking settings (defaults until saved: version null)
GET {{baseUrl}}/salon/settings
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

> {%
    if (response.status === 200) {
        // written into the JSON as-is, so null must be the text "null"
        client.global.set("settingsVersion", response.body.version === null ? "null" : response.body.version);
    }
%}

### 6k. Salon: save booking settings (send the version from 6j; null on the first save)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/salon/settings
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "version": {{settingsVersion}}, "minLeadMinutes": 60, "maxDaysAhead": 14 }

> {%
    if (response.status === 200) {
        client.global.set("settingsVersion", response.body.version);
    }
%}

### 7. Upload a bill photo (needs a shop: register in 6b and refresh first, otherwise 403 SHOP_REQUIRED)
POST {{baseUrl}}/files
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=ApniDukan

--ApniDukan
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="purpose"

BILL
--ApniDukan
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="bill.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./sample-bill.jpg
--ApniDukan--

> {%
    if (response.status === 200 || response.status === 201) {
        client.global.set("fileId", response.body.id);
    }
%}

### 8. Link to view a file for 5 minutes (add ?download=true to save it instead)
GET {{baseUrl}}/files/{{fileId}}/link
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 9. Delete a file (Neon + R2)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/files/{{fileId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 10. Sign out this device
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}" }

### 11. Registration step 2: upload the owner's photo (any JPEG; reuses sample-bill.jpg here)
POST {{baseUrl}}/files
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=ApniDukan

--ApniDukan
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="purpose"

OWNER_PHOTO
--ApniDukan
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="owner.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./sample-bill.jpg
--ApniDukan--

> {%
    if (response.status === 200 || response.status === 201) {
        client.global.set("ownerPhotoId", response.body.id);
    }
%}

### 11b. ... and a photo of the shop (purpose SHOP_PHOTO; use a different picture than 11)
POST {{baseUrl}}/files
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=ApniDukan

--ApniDukan
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="purpose"

SHOP_PHOTO
--ApniDukan
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="shop.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./sample-bill.jpg
--ApniDukan--

> {%
    if (response.status === 200 || response.status === 201) {
        client.global.set("shopPhotoId", response.body.id);
    }
%}

### 11c. Set both photos on My shop (run 6c first for the version)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/shops/me/photos
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "version": {{shopVersion}}, "ownerPhotoFileId": "{{ownerPhotoId}}", "shopPhotoFileId": "{{shopPhotoId}}" }

> {%
    if (response.status === 200) {
        client.global.set("shopVersion", response.body.version);
    }
%}

### 11d. Submit for visit (409 PHOTOS_REQUIRED until both photos are set)
POST {{baseUrl}}/shops/me/submit
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "version": {{shopVersion}} }

> {%
    if (response.status === 200) {
        client.global.set("shopVersion", response.body.version);
    }
%}

### 11e. Field team only (users.admin_role ADMIN or SUPER_ADMIN): shops waiting for a visit, with photo links. Saves the first one.
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/shops
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

> {%
    if (response.status === 200 && response.body.length > 0) {
        client.global.set("adminShopId", response.body[0].id);
        client.global.set("adminShopVersion", response.body[0].version);
    }
%}

### 11f. Field team: approve that shop after the visit, with the version you checked (409 SHOP_CHANGED if not)
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/shops/{{adminShopId}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "version": {{adminShopVersion}} }

### 11g. Field team: or send it back after the visit (PENDING_VISIT → DRAFT); the owner sees the reason in 6c
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/shops/{{adminShopId}}/reject
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "version": {{adminShopVersion}}, "reason": "The shop photo doesn't show the shop's name board." }

### 11h. Field team: live shops. Saves the first one.
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/shops?status=APPROVED
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

> {%
    if (response.status === 200 && response.body.length > 0) {
        client.global.set("adminShopId", response.body[0].id);
        client.global.set("adminShopVersion", response.body[0].version);
    }
%}

### 11i. Field team: suspend it (off the app; a salon's upcoming online bookings are cancelled, customers told)
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/shops/{{adminShopId}}/suspend
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "version": {{adminShopVersion}}, "reason": "Customers report the shop closed for weeks." }

> {%
    client.global.set("adminShopVersion", response.body.version);
%}

### 11j. Field team: end the suspension (back to PENDING_VISIT; approve with 11e-11f after checking again)
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/shops/{{adminShopId}}/reinstate
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "version": {{adminShopVersion}} }

### 12. Salon: give barber Raju (6g) his own sign-in with his phone
PUT {{baseUrl}}/salon/staff/{{staffId}}/login
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "phone": "{{barberPhone}}" }

### 12a. Owner: add a helper by phone (they sign in with OTP and find the shop); then list everyone
POST {{baseUrl}}/shops/me/helpers
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "phone": "{{helperPhone}}" }

### 12a2. Owner: everyone in the shop (name, phone, role)
GET {{baseUrl}}/shops/me/members
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 12b. Salon: everyone in the salon, and who may add walk-ins
GET {{baseUrl}}/salon/members
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 13. Customer: salons near a point (the salon must be approved, 11f)
GET {{baseUrl}}/salons?lat=17.466&lng=78.365
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

> {%
    if (response.status === 200 && response.body.length > 0) {
        client.global.set("salonId", response.body[0].id);
    }
%}

### 13b. Customer: free times for the haircut (6e) on a date (India date)
GET {{baseUrl}}/salons/{{salonId}}/availability?services={{serviceId}}&date={{bookingDate}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

> {%
    if (response.status === 200 && response.body.starts.length > 0) {
        client.global.set("startAt", response.body.starts[0].startAt);
    }
%}

### 13c. Customer: book the first free time. A new Idempotency-Key per booking; the same one when retrying
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$random.uuid}}

{ "salonId": "{{salonId}}", "serviceIds": ["{{serviceId}}"], "startAt": "{{startAt}}" }

> {%
    if (response.status === 201) {
        client.global.set("bookingId", response.body.id);
        client.global.set("startCode", response.body.startCode);
    }
%}

### 13d. Customer: my upcoming bookings (with the start code)
GET {{baseUrl}}/me/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 14. Salon: the day screen
GET {{baseUrl}}/salon/day?date={{bookingDate}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 14a. Salon: everything coming up across the next days, soonest first (owner and helpers see customer phones)
GET {{baseUrl}}/salon/upcoming
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 14b. Salon: walk-in suggestions for the haircut
GET {{baseUrl}}/salon/walk-ins/options?services={{serviceId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 14b2. Salon: add a walk-in with a barber who is free now; it starts at once (no code). A new Idempotency-Key each time
POST {{baseUrl}}/salon/walk-ins
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$random.uuid}}

{ "serviceIds": ["{{serviceId}}"], "staffId": "{{staffId}}", "name": "Walk-in" }

### 14c. Salon: start the booking with the customer's code (from 15 minutes before its time)
POST {{baseUrl}}/salon/appointments/{{bookingId}}/start
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "{{startCode}}" }

### 14d. Customer: cancel a booking that hasn't started (book another with 13c first; after 14c this one is 409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings/{{bookingId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 14e. Salon: pause online bookings until midnight / resume
POST {{baseUrl}}/salon/pause
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 14f. Salon: resume online bookings
POST {{baseUrl}}/salon/resume
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 15. Customer: move my booking to another free start (take one from 13b)
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings/{{bookingId}}/reschedule
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "startAt": "{{startAt}}" }

### 15b. Customer: set my name (salons see it)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Ravi" }

### 15c. Customer: allow notifications on this device (the app sends the browser's PushSubscription)
GET {{baseUrl}}/push/public-key
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 16. Salon: No-show (from 15 minutes after the start)
POST {{baseUrl}}/salon/appointments/{{bookingId}}/no-show
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 16a. Salon: undo a No-show (owner or helper, within 24 hours): the strike goes, the booking is closed, the customer is told
POST {{baseUrl}}/salon/appointments/{{bookingId}}/undo-no-show
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 16a2. Salon: done before the planned end (frees the rest of the barber's time)
POST {{baseUrl}}/salon/appointments/{{bookingId}}/finish
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 16b. Salon: give the booking (or a walk-in in the chair) to another barber
POST {{baseUrl}}/salon/appointments/{{bookingId}}/reassign
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "staffId": "{{staffId}}" }

### 16c. Salon: a break for barber Raju (times are exact moments; 08:30Z = 2:00 PM in India)
POST {{baseUrl}}/salon/staff/{{staffId}}/blocks
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "BREAK", "startAt": "{{bookingDate}}T08:30:00Z", "endAt": "{{bookingDate}}T09:00:00Z" }

### 16d. Salon: close the whole salon for a day (409 BLOCK_CONFLICTS lists bookings in the way)
POST {{baseUrl}}/salon/closures
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "date": "{{bookingDate}}" }

### 16e. Salon: switch barber Raju off (he left) or on again; send his version from GET /salon/staff
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/salon/staff/{{staffId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "version": {{staffVersion}}, "active": false }

### 17. Support only (users.admin = true): a customer's strikes and whether booking is blocked, by phone
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/salon/strikes/lookup
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "phone": "{{phone}}" }

### 17b. Support: take back the strike of a booking, with the reason (kept in the booking's history)
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/salon/strikes/{{bookingId}}/remove
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Customer was in the chair; the barber pressed No-show by mistake." }

### 18. Delete my account, step 1: a code to my own phone (409 SHOP_OWNER for a shop owner). Put it in "otp".
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/me/delete-code
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 18b. Step 2: deletes the account for good (204) and signs out every device. Use a test phone, not yours!
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/me/delete
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "{{otp}}" }

### 19. Owner: the salon's history for a range of India dates (at most 31 days)
GET {{baseUrl}}/salon/history?from={{bookingDate}}&to={{bookingDate}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 19b. Owner: remove a helper (put their user id from 12a2 in "helperId")
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/shops/me/helpers/{{helperId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 19c. A helper or barber: leave the shop
POST {{baseUrl}}/shops/me/leave
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 19d. Sign out of every device
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout-all
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 19e. Health check (no sign-in; what Railway calls)
GET {{host}}/actuator/health

### 20. My messages in the app (customer app; ?app=partner for the salon's)
GET {{baseUrl}}/me/notifications
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 20b. How many are unread (for the bell)
GET {{baseUrl}}/me/notifications/unread-count
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 20c. Mark everything read (send {"ids": ["..."]} to mark only some)
POST {{baseUrl}}/me/notifications/read
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 21. Admin website: who I am, my role, and whether OTP test mode is on
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 21b. Dashboard: kiranas and salons in each group
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/dashboard
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 21c. Salons waiting for their first visit (q: shop number, name or owner phone)
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/shops?type=SALON&group=FIRST_VISIT&q=
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

> {%
    if (response.body.length > 0) {
        client.global.set("adminShopId", response.body[0].id);
        client.global.set("adminShopVersion", response.body[0].version);
    }
%}

### 21d. One shop: what changed since approval, and its timeline
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/shops/{{adminShopId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 21e. Send back with a checklist, a reason for the owner and a note only admins see
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/shops/{{adminShopId}}/reject
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "version": {{adminShopVersion}}, "reason": "The pin is not at the shop.", "note": "Called the owner, no answer.",
  "checklist": ["PIN_WRONG"] }

### 21f. A note on the timeline (admins only)
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/shops/{{adminShopId}}/notes
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "note": "Shop is behind the temple; call before going." }

### 21g. Super admin: the team; add an admin by phone
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/team
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/team
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "phone": "9000000002" }

### 21h. Super admin: add a test number, then OTP test mode on for 2 hours (and off)
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/test-mode/phones
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "phone": "9111111111", "label": "My test barber" }

###
PUT {{baseUrl}}/admin/test-mode
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "hours": 2 }

###
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/admin/test-mode
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
